<title>JAPAN: Japan firms win Y35 bln monorail order in Malaysia.</title>
<headline>Japan firms win Y35 bln monorail order in Malaysia.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toyo Engineering Corp said on Wednesday that it, Itochu Corp and Hitachi Ltd have won an order to build a monorail system in Malaysia.</p>
<p>The order is worth about 35 billion yen, a Toyo Engineering spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The 15-km long inner-city monorail system in Kuala Lumpur will be built by KL PRT Sdn Bhd.</p>
<p>The construction of the monorail is expected to be completed at the end of December 1999.</p>
<p>The construction is aimed at easing traffic congestion in the Malaysian capital.</p>
</text>
